  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Plotting the graph of the function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis, we get</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0090_f7268db1569d.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 151px;\" /></p><p>Now applying the formula of area of trapezium which is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>height</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mtext>sum&#160;of&#160;parallel&#160;sides</mtext></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p>Required area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Trap</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
